{"id": "EUVD-2026-86138", "enisaUuid": "f8bb6241-e5cb-3872-9184-7edca8137d1c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: RSI: fix field-spanning write warning in attestation token init\n\nThe challenge is passed in registers a1 through a8. However, copying to\n&regs.a1 makes FORTIFY treat the destination as the single a1 field,\nresulting in a field-spanning write warning. [1]\n\nOverlay the SMCCC register structure with an RSI-specific argument\nlayout and copy the challenge into an explicit 64-byte array. This keeps\nthe existing a1-a8 argument encoding while giving the copy a correctly\nsized destination object.\n\n[1]\nmemcpy: detected field-spanning write (size 64) of single field \"&regs.a1\" at ./arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h:119 (size 8)\nWARNING: ./arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h:119 at rsi_attestation_token_init+0xdc/0xf8 [arm_cca_guest], CPU#0: cat/3314", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:52:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e505092cb200d430d5b8d8d3e926d45f29474ba3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d29a8ee271da17b5e32d7a76a9c78d43f66447ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/221049874b6a78c7d87bc826581b0695cd338e2b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xvwh-h3f9-mq6w", "CVE-2026-93266"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f335496-11f7-3090-9f60-ea29277e3cae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "260660fc-9021-3e42-90c3-58d97661c4c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "66a5338f-be35-30d5-b3f5-6846b3ef44ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b880a80011f56880f32bde47fc6af313359f926b <d29a8ee271da17b5e32d7a76a9c78d43f66447ca"}, {"id": "988f1645-6779-32a8-ab77-6f2a2ee77936", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b880a80011f56880f32bde47fc6af313359f926b <221049874b6a78c7d87bc826581b0695cd338e2b"}, {"id": "b1e24547-9fda-300c-978e-9e87bd71b6fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "d62601c4-0d10-30eb-887b-27fc3d67c494", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b880a80011f56880f32bde47fc6af313359f926b <e505092cb200d430d5b8d8d3e926d45f29474ba3"}, {"id": "e0f868ed-7fe1-36a6-bb2d-37cfe8dc6abe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "eb9401b2-5103-30ab-a1c0-4fee98574a85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "90d4d88b-6a19-307b-b16e-dce720d0e69d", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}